<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     TIME DIFFERENCE SECTION & SIDE-BY-SIDE GRAPHIC
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section" id="time-difference" aria-labelledby="time-diff-heading">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Time Difference Mechanics</p>
    <h2 id="time-diff-heading">Analyzing the Time Gap: AEST vs EST</h2>
    <p>
      The time difference between Australian Eastern Standard Time (AEST) and US Eastern Standard Time (EST) is exactly <strong>15 hours</strong>. Since AEST operates at UTC+10 and EST is fixed at UTC-5, eastern Australia runs fifteen hours ahead of Eastern Standard Time. When it is 8:00 AM EST in New York during winter, local clocks in Sydney and Melbourne show 11:00 PM AEST on the same calendar day.
    </p>
    <p>
      This time difference shifts when daylight saving rules apply. The United Kingdom and New Zealand observe daylight saving time on opposite cycles because they are located in different hemispheres. When Australia switches to AEDT (UTC+11) and the US is on EST (UTC-5), the gap increases to 16 hours. Conversely, when Australia returns to AEST (UTC+10) and the US shifts to Eastern Daylight Time (EDT, UTC-4), the gap narrows to 14 hours.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Custom AEST vs EST Comparison Infographic (SVG) -->
  <div style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 700px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px;">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 600 200" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
      <rect width="600" height="200" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
      
      <!-- Side by Side Visual Clocks -->
      <g transform="translate(100, 100)">
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="60" fill="#12455d" stroke="#2f6278" stroke-width="4" />
        <!-- AEST Clock Hands show 10:00 -->
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="-30" y2="-30" stroke="#f4fbff" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-45" stroke="#bdd2dc" stroke-width="2" />
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="5" fill="#36c7b5" />
        <text x="0" y="85" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="16" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">AEST Time (UTC+10)</text>
      </g>

      <g transform="translate(300, 100)">
        <text x="0" y="10" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="32" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">←</text>
        <rect x="-45" y="-35" width="90" height="26" rx="13" fill="#1b536e" />
        <text x="0" y="-17" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">-15 HOURS</text>
      </g>

      <g transform="translate(500, 100)">
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="60" fill="#12455d" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="4" />
        <!-- EST is -15 hours behind AEST, so hands show 7:00 on standard winter -->
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="-30" y2="30" stroke="#f4fbff" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-45" stroke="#8fd7ff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="5" fill="#36c7b5" />
        <text x="0" y="85" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="16" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">EST Time (UTC-5)</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>AEST Standard (UTC+10)</h3>
      <p>Australian Eastern Standard Time covers Queensland, New South Wales, Victoria, Tasmania, and the ACT, positioning eastern Australia 10 hours ahead of the prime meridian.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>EST Standard (UTC−5)</h3>
      <p>Eastern Standard Time is the winter civil baseline for New York, Washington D.C., Toronto, Boston, and Miami, located 5 hours behind Greenwich Mean Time.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Opposite DST Cycles</h3>
      <p>Because the Northern and Southern Hemispheres experience opposite seasons, the gap oscillates between 14 hours (US summer), 15 hours (standard), and 16 hours (AU summer).</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

